  - name: "cyber-audit-lab"
abstract: >-
  Aggregate results of an exploratory study of the names that 84 language models from 20 families (including
  GPT-2 and Pythia as pre-chat comparisons and three diffusion language models) choose when asked to name themselves, with matched control prompts,
  prompt-variation sets, follow-up explanations, model probabilities, answers that name another AI, and a comparison
  of reasoning before a choice with the explanation given afterwards (736,408 answers). Includes a findings report,
  aggregate tables, figures, prompts and a paper (the paper describes version 1.2). No full answers or per-answer records. Exploratory: no
  pre-registration was frozen before collection.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - self-naming
  - model identity
  - output diversity
  - mode collapse
  - post-training
